# Example ReRDMFT input file: Ne, cc-pVDZ, FUNCTIONAL PCCD, C4_DHF with the 4-component min-max
# stage (FULL_OPTIMIZATION_4C_NEG TRUE) -- same no-pair pCCD minimum as ne_pccd_c4.inp, then NEO
# extends the orbital rotations to the positive<->negative-energy pairs and converges to the
# saddle point (Talman 1986/Saue ChemPhysChem 2011's min-max characterization), re-solving the
# pCCD amplitudes at the new orbitals, macro-iterated. CHOLESKY TRUE keeps it cheap (under 2 min).
#
# Converged total energies:
#   C4_DHF (no-pair, positive-energy-only minimum): -128.7027634 Hartree
#   C4_DHF (min-max, including the negative-energy spinors): -128.7027634 Hartree
#     (-6.689e-09 Hartree relative to the no-pair minimum -- the physically expected tiny scale
#     of positive<->negative-energy mixing, O(1/c^2); see also lih_gnof_c4_neg_full_optimization.inp
#     and lih_muller_c4_neg_full_optimization_cholesky.inp for the same scale on a different
#     functional/system).
#
# This example only converges cleanly since the pCCD amplitude warm-up bug was fixed (the
# amplitude cache used to be pre-populated at the UNROTATED starting integrals instead of the
# no-pair minimum's own rotated ones, a basis mismatch that made NEO's very first trust-region
# step wildly oversized and the whole min-max search diverge catastrophically within the first
# macro-iteration -- confirmed on both LiH/6-31G and this system before the fix).
NELEC 10
BASIS ne-cc-pvdz.gbs
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
X2C TRUE
C4_SPINOR TRUE
FUNCTIONAL PCCD
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
FULL_OPTIMIZATION_4C_NEG TRUE
CHOLESKY TRUE

GEOMETRY
Ne  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
END
